the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/f4/f41802149d3e2a8524a47123e6de1bb6aa68e480cf54aafd756085ad52355ede.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $\\angle CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overrightarrow{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(\\angle BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $\\angle CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(\\angle BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(\\angle BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx = 90^\\circ - 35^\\circ = 55^\\circ.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9a3a7198-9475-534b-8bac-8c66e26d7479" "question-fef21b13-21e0-5738-b7d2-5549afbbc9e6" "question-d11aa747-bb6b-58c1-bf80-7ecc88be04aa" "question-e0ae28b7-07ff-5372-8c05-3a6fb2ad772e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110382 :question/problem "In the figure below, $m \\angle BAE = {110}^{\\circ}.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/24/245dbaa430eb99aee193110fcd6df2844cfd7cffd2363c561337ac74d18a1fb5.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $\\angle CAD.$\n\nThe measure of $\\angle CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(\\angle BAE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle DAE).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx = 110^\\circ - 40^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 50^\\circ.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-04351232-e12f-56c5-9996-c18094808c54" :question/id #uuid "04351232-e12f-56c5-9996-c18094808c54" :question/math-academy-id "q-154716" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c5a57e090562c65ff7f0ff8d7c63f469a038d4396bba68be3cb4916f4e7aab7.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $\\overset{^}{COE}?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/18/18be9d5946a70aa62b4dda5408fa7e3312fe2e33675cbf695cbbdecac2feaa5b.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\overset{^}{COD}$ and $\\overset{^}{DOE}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OD}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\overset{^}{COE} & =m\\overset{^}{COD}+m\\overset{^}{DOE} \\\\  & ={70}^{∘}+{35}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5bad39f7-11be-5684-b61f-14d08753ac2c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5bad39f7-11be-5684-b61f-14d08753ac2c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bad39f7-11be-5684-b61f-14d08753ac2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49734c3c-e905-5965-849c-4608b2744957" :answer-field/choices ["answer-43e8f4df-924a-5f52-ab86-c66b86fd7066" "answer-49734c3c-e905-5965-849c-4608b2744957" "answer-d9d128b2-4dc7-59f5-9ae4-fde84a06094e" "answer-9c698d28-82ec-5692-8e2d-00b41b67219b" "answer-c90f3de1-1357-5463-ae42-347f8c096902"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43e8f4df-924a-5f52-ab86-c66b86fd7066" :answer/id #uuid "43e8f4df-924a-5f52-ab86-c66b86fd7066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{102}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49734c3c-e905-5965-849c-4608b2744957" :answer/id #uuid "49734c3c-e905-5965-849c-4608b2744957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9d128b2-4dc7-59f5-9ae4-fde84a06094e" :answer/id #uuid "d9d128b2-4dc7-59f5-9ae4-fde84a06094e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c698d28-82ec-5692-8e2d-00b41b67219b" :answer/id #uuid "9c698d28-82ec-5692-8e2d-00b41b67219b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{122}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c90f3de1-1357-5463-ae42-347f8c096902"