 the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={100}^{∘}-{70}^{∘}={30}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72353706-d84b-5582-8ba8-ead7370acdc5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72353706-d84b-5582-8ba8-ead7370acdc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "72353706-d84b-5582-8ba8-ead7370acdc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af12c256-412b-55f2-ab62-1d721dbffd84" "answer-f0073151-722a-59a3-b73c-920d6bd1dd42" "answer-7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" "answer-639e261a-02d5-509d-8b25-6646fedeecf6" "answer-8e013960-5f20-5489-8ad0-1fda062c79f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af12c256-412b-55f2-ab62-1d721dbffd84" :answer/id #uuid "af12c256-412b-55f2-ab62-1d721dbffd84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{170}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0073151-722a-59a3-b73c-920d6bd1dd42" :answer/id #uuid "f0073151-722a-59a3-b73c-920d6bd1dd42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" :answer/id #uuid "7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-639e261a-02d5-509d-8b25-6646fedeecf6" :answer/id #uuid "639e261a-02d5-509d-8b25-6646fedeecf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e013960-5f20-5489-8ad0-1fda062c79f4" :answer/id #uuid "8e013960-5f20-5489-8ad0-1fda062c79f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e497b6b9-99ae-5a25-8d57-b87ff9f54120" :question/id #uuid "e497b6b9-99ae-5a25-8d57-b87ff9f54120" :question/math-academy-id "q-150770" :question/problem "![](images/51/51504155eb8a1886004062bc3f14845119f2e8f669273aece8cf4772c9a51d42.png)\n\nThe measure of the angle $∠LON$ is ${120}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠MON.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠LOM$ and $∠MON$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OM}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠LON)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠LOM$ and $∠MON).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠MON$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠LON)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠LOM).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={120}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}={70}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8edb448b-4874-58ed-9c0f-e4042edce6b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8edb448b-4874-58ed-9c0f-e4042edce6b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "8edb448b-4874-58ed-9c0f-e4042edce6b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-522cb4ec-eb5a-56f1-a309-7a056515cc3b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dbd31e59-040c-5ef8-a5b7-14130a70862b" "answer-bc0bca5b-166f-514b-a8a3-5ba18d5b837f" "answer-62340687-3fc2-5a2f-944a-909d5d677a7c" "answer-522cb4ec-eb5a-56f1-a309-7a056515cc3b" "answer-7c07917a-7943-5a65-a206-fc4404e131fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbd31e59-040c-5ef8-a5b7-14130a70862b" :answer/id #uuid "dbd31e59-040c-5ef8-a5b7-14130a70862b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [